# .bobignore — what IBM Bob may not read in this repo.
#
# gitignore syntax. Bob blocks read_file, write_file, apply_diff and
# GetSymbolsOverview against these, and blocks execute_command for a predefined
# list of file-reading commands.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT: a security boundary. IBM's own docs say insert_content and
# search_and_replace "might bypass .bobignore rules" on the final write, and the
# execute_command protection covers only a fixed list of commands. So this is a
# filter, not a wall. The actual boundary is which folder Bob is opened in:
# this repo is the hackathon and is the only thing Bob may ever see.

# ── credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example is placeholders only (checked), and Bob needs it to understand
# the configuration surface. Every other .env is real and is not its business.
.env*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# ── 360MB that would be read at your expense ─────────────────────────────────
# The trial carries 40 Bobcoins and every interaction spends them. node_modules
# is 357MB and dist is 3.5MB of generated output; neither tells Bob anything
# about this codebase that src/ does not say better.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/

# Generated, large, and the npm-vs-Bun question is still open on the team, so
# neither lockfile is authoritative to reason from.
bun.lock
package-lock.json

*.log
.DS_Store
